Sort First:
  - prepass geometry, bin by position
  - then redistribute bins to do geometry and pixel on one partition

  For e.g., you can do position only geometry as part of the prepass geometry stage

Sort Middle:
  - Geometry distributed randomly or streamed using some load heuristics
  - redistribution happens after G when screen space partitions are known
  - each Rasterizer owns 1+ bins

  This is your everyday Graphics hardware

Sort Last:
  - General E2E G/R images
  - Redistribute pixels
  - Composite globally

  Can either globally communicate z/stencil and send out surviving pixels from each Partition or
  send out full image from each partition and do a global z/stencil in one quadrant
  (Former makes more sense aka build a global consensus on z/stencil and have each Partition reject
  its own before sending out)

 and like everything else you can mix-n-match these key concepts to build something smarter :-)


